5 shall be held in the name of the state of Wyoming and shall
6 be administered by the board of land commissioners. Funds
7 deposited within the trust account are intended to be
8 inviolate and constitute a perpetual trust account which
9 shall be invested by The state treasurer, as authorized by
10 law and in a manner to obtain the highest net return
11 possible consistent with preservation of the account corpus
12 or his designee, who shall be registered under the
13 Investment Advisor's Act of 1940, as amended, if required
14 to be registered by the terms of that act, as amended, may
15 invest the unobligated, unencumbered balance of the trust
16 account in equities, including stocks of corporations.
17 Investments under this subsection shall be in accordance
18 with W.S. 9-4-715(a) and (c) through (e) and 9-4-716. In
